"**Keep the relative clause next to its antecedent:** <s>He gave a book to the boy which was torn.</s> (ambiguous) → *He gave the boy **a book which was torn**.* · <s>I met a girl in the park who was singing.</s> → *I met **a girl who was singing** in the park.*",
"**Commas matter for meaning:** *My brother **who lives in Pune** is a doctor.* (I have more than one brother) · *My brother, **who lives in Pune**, is a doctor.* (I have only one)",
